# Pi keeps hand-edited config and generated runtime state side by side in ~/.pi.
# Deny everything by default so a Pi upgrade dropping a new state file next to
# settings.json does not get silently committed. Allow back only real config.
# Leading slashes matter: a bare `*` would also match inside agent/themes/ and
# swallow the theme files that the rules below try to allow back.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/agent/
/agent/*
!/agent/settings.json
# Personal instructions live in AGENTS.md, deliberately NOT SYSTEM.md: pi *replaces*
# its whole default system prompt with SYSTEM.md, so a preferences file there silently
# drops every tool-usage instruction pi ships with. AGENTS.md layers instead.
# Use APPEND_SYSTEM.md only for rules that must sit above project context files.
!/agent/AGENTS.md
!/agent/APPEND_SYSTEM.md
!/agent/models.json
!/agent/keybindings.json
!/agent/mcp.json
!/agent/themes/
!/supi

# The experimental RLM profile, selected by PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=~/.pi/agent-rlm
# (the `pii` fish abbr). Everything else in it is a symlink back to agent/.
!/agent-rlm/
/agent-rlm/*
!/agent-rlm/settings.json
!/agent-rlm/README.md
!/agent-rlm/AGENTS.md
!/agent-rlm/lib/
!/agent-rlm/docs/

# Deliberately NOT tracked (all of the above is denied by `*`, listed here as the record):
#   agent/auth.json          - provider credentials
#   agent/trust.json         - per-machine directory trust allowlist
#   agent/models-store.json  - fetched provider model catalogue
#   agent/mcp-cache.json     - MCP server capability cache
#   agent/mcp-npx-cache.json - npx resolution cache
#   agent/run-history.jsonl  - local run history
#   agent/sessions/          - conversation transcripts
#   agent/npm/               - extensions installed from settings.json `packages`
#   agent/git/               - clones of extensions installed via `pi install git:...`
#   agent-rlm/sessions/      - RLM-profile conversation transcripts
#   context-mode/            - context-mode SQLite databases
